<%# Slug-change decision modal — shown by editor#save BEFORE the form submits,
    when a PUBLISHED post's url_name was edited. Nothing has been saved yet, so
    all three choices are honest:
      • Create redirect & save — save the rename and write a 301 (old → new)
      • Keep old URL           — revert the slug field, then save (no redirect)
      • Cancel                 — close, save nothing
    Hidden until the editor reveals it and fills in the from/to paths. %>
<div id="redirect-decision-modal"
     data-editor-target="redirectModal"
     class="hidden fixed inset-0 bg-amber-700/35 flex items-center justify-center z-50">
  <div class="bg-white border-2 border-gray-900 p-8 max-w-lg mx-auto">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">You changed this post's URL</h2>

    <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
      This post is published, so anyone who linked to the old address will hit a
      dead page unless you forward it.
    </p>

    <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-300 p-4 mb-4 text-sm font-mono space-y-1">
      <div><span class="text-gray-500">old&nbsp;</span><span data-editor-target="redirectFrom"></span></div>
      <div><span class="text-gray-500">new&nbsp;</span><span data-editor-target="redirectTo"></span></div>
    </div>

    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-6">
      <%# Names the OTHER side of Site Sync: editing on local syncs to live, and
          editing on the live site syncs back to local. %>
      A redirect will be added to <span class="font-mono">Settings → Roe → redirects.yml</span>
      and syncs to your <%= Rails.env.production? ? "local" : "live" %> site.
    </p>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3">
      <%# Cancel sits apart on the left: nothing is saved, back to the editor. %>
      <button type="button"
              data-action="click->editor#cancelRedirectDecision"
              class="uppercase text-sm px-4 py-2 border border-gray-800 bg-white hover:bg-gray-100 font-mono rounded-xs cursor-pointer text-nowrap">
        Cancel<span class="hidden sm:inline"> — keep editing</span>
      </button>

      <%# The two ways to SAVE, grouped on the right. Both commit your edits; they
          differ only in what happens to the URL. %>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <button type="button"
                data-action="click->editor#keepOldUrlAndSave"
                class="uppercase text-sm px-4 py-2 border border-gray-800 bg-gray-200 hover:bg-gray-100 font-mono rounded-xs cursor-pointer text-nowrap">
          Save with old URL
        </button>
        <button type="button"
                data-action="click->editor#createRedirectAndSave"
                class="uppercase text-sm px-4 py-2 border border-gray-800 bg-green-200 hover:bg-green-300 font-mono rounded-xs cursor-pointer text-nowrap">
          Save new URL &amp; redirect
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# Plain-language legend so the three choices can't be confused. %>
    <ul class="mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-gray-200 text-xs text-gray-500 space-y-1">
      <li><span class="font-semibold text-gray-700">Save new URL &amp; redirect</span> — use the new address and forward the old one so existing links keep working.</li>
      <li><span class="font-semibold text-gray-700">Save with old URL</span> — keep the previously saved address (undo just the rename) and save your other edits.</li>
      <li><span class="font-semibold text-gray-700">Cancel</span> — don't save anything; go back to the editor.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>
